('CAREFUL_READING', '<h4>Ocean Acidification</h4><p>Ocean acidification, sometimes called "climate change evil twin," occurs when excess carbon dioxide in the atmosphere dissolves into seawater, forming carbonic acid and lowering the ocean pH. Since the Industrial Revolution, the average pH of surface ocean waters has fallen by 0.1 units, representing a 30% increase in acidity. If current emission trends continue, ocean acidity could increase by 150% by 2100.</p><p>The impacts on marine life are already evident. Shell-forming organisms—including oysters, clams, and corals—struggle to build and maintain their calcium carbonate structures in more acidic waters. Coral reefs, which support approximately 25% of marine biodiversity, face a dual threat from warming waters that cause bleaching and acidification that weakens their skeletons. Pteropods, tiny marine snails at the base of many ocean food webs, show visible shell dissolution in affected waters.</p><p>The socioeconomic consequences are substantial. Global fisheries and aquaculture provide protein for over 3 billion people and livelihoods for hundreds of millions. The degradation of coral reefs threatens not only marine biodiversity but also coastal protection and tourism revenue for many tropical nations. Unlike some climate impacts that can be locally managed, ocean acidification is a global problem that requires global reductions in carbon dioxide emissions to address.</p>',
 NULL, 'PASSAGE', '', 7, '仔细阅读,海洋酸化,气候'),
('CAREFUL_READING', 'By how much has ocean surface pH fallen since the Industrial Revolution?', '[{"label":"A","text":"0.01 units"},{"label":"B","text":"0.1 units"},{"label":"C","text":"1.0 units"},{"label":"D","text":"5.0 units"}]', 'B', '第一段: "fallen by 0.1 units, representing a 30% increase in acidity."', 6, '仔细阅读,细节'),
('CAREFUL_READING', 'Why are pteropods important?', '[{"label":"A","text":"They are a popular food fish"},{"label":"B","text":"They sit at the base of many ocean food chains"},{"label":"C","text":"They produce oxygen"},{"label":"D","text":"They are used in medicine"}]', 'B', '第二段: "tiny marine snails at the base of many ocean food webs."', 6, '仔细阅读,细节'),
('CAREFUL_READING', 'How many people depend on fisheries for protein?', '[{"label":"A","text":"About 100 million"},{"label":"B","text":"About 1 billion"},{"label":"C","text":"Over 3 billion"},{"label":"D","text":"Over 7 billion"}]', 'C', '第三段: "provide protein for over 3 billion people."', 6, '仔细阅读,细节'),
('CAREFUL_READING', 'Unlike some local climate impacts, ocean acidification requires:', '[{"label":"A","text":"Only local solutions"},{"label":"B","text":"Global reductions in carbon dioxide emissions"},{"label":"C","text":"No action at all"},{"label":"D","text":"Only technological solutions"}]', 'B', '末段: "a global problem that requires global reductions in carbon dioxide emissions to address."', 7, '仔细阅读,推理');

